WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.115 --> 00:00:18.558
morning, the Earthworms rode their bikes to the end of Old Church Road.

2
00:00:19.639 --> 00:00:20.899
Katie was confused.

3
00:00:20.919 --> 00:00:23.801
"Do we go this way or that way?"

4
00:00:24.261 --> 00:00:24.841
she asked.

5
00:00:24.861 --> 00:00:26.622
"We need a GPS!"

6
00:00:27.923 --> 00:00:29.044
But Luke knew the way.

7
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.802
He led them over an old bridge and down a dirt road.

8
00:00:33.822 --> 00:00:35.742
"We're getting close!"

9
00:00:36.963 --> 00:00:40.364
A few moments later, they stopped in front of an old house.

10
00:00:41.465 --> 00:00:43.005
"This is it," he said.

11
00:00:43.505 --> 00:00:44.566
It looked deserted.

12
00:00:44.586 --> 00:00:47.847
"Creepy," said Katie.

13
00:00:47.867 --> 00:00:51.669
"Nobody lives here," said Emily.

14
00:00:51.689 --> 00:00:55.530
"Let's go home," said AJ.

15
00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:59.412
"Shh. Listen," said Emily.

16
00:01:00.028 --> 00:01:01.169
Someone was singing.

17
00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:08.613
They left their bikes and followed the voice.

18
00:01:09.794 --> 00:01:14.016
An old woman was hanging clothes to dry, singing as she worked.

19
00:01:15.577 --> 00:01:20.820
She fastened the last piece to the line, picked up her basket, and turned around.

20
00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:22.901
"Who are you?"

21
00:01:23.521 --> 00:01:24.182
she snapped.

22
00:01:25.403 --> 00:01:27.624
"She seems crabby," thought Katie.

23
00:01:28.864 --> 00:01:30.205
"We're the Earthworms!"

24
00:01:30.806 --> 00:01:31.547
said AJ.

25
00:01:32.047 --> 00:01:33.228
Emily pushed her brother.

26
00:01:33.248 --> 00:01:36.270
"I'm Emily," she said.

27
00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:39.233
"Luke." "AJ."

28
00:01:39.253 --> 00:01:43.056
"Katie." "What are you doing here?

29
00:01:43.076 --> 00:01:47.079
I never have visitors," the old woman said.

30
00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:51.323
"We're on a scavenger hunt," Katie replied.

31
00:01:52.704 --> 00:01:54.125
The woman looked doubtful.

32
00:01:54.145 --> 00:01:56.888
"What are you hunting out here?"

33
00:01:58.180 --> 00:01:59.841
"You!" said AJ.

34
00:01:59.861 --> 00:02:04.564
"The oldest person in Willow Creek," said Emily.

35
00:02:04.584 --> 00:02:06.365
"You're Ms.

36
00:02:06.445 --> 00:02:08.006
Cora Mae Henderson, right?"

37
00:02:08.446 --> 00:02:09.106
said Katie.

38
00:02:09.126 --> 00:02:12.929
"Your brother drew us a map so we could find you."

39
00:02:12.949 --> 00:02:17.471
"My brother is a busybody," said Ms.

40
00:02:17.491 --> 00:02:20.933
Henderson. "He has a Model T!"

41
00:02:21.394 --> 00:02:22.154
said AJ.

42
00:02:23.275 --> 00:02:25.276
Ms. Henderson finally smiled.

43
00:02:26.293 --> 00:02:27.013
"Oh, yes.

44
00:02:27.574 --> 00:02:29.375
I've heard all about it.

45
00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:33.579
Brother says he will take me for a ride soon."

46
00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:37.122
Ms. Henderson looked up at the back porch.

47
00:02:37.142 --> 00:02:41.025
"If you don't mind, I'd like to sit down."

48
00:02:42.466 --> 00:02:49.332
When everyone was comfortable, Luke said, "Your brother says his Model T was the first car in Willow

49
00:02:49.432 --> 00:02:53.416
Creek." "That could be true," she said.

50
00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:59.302
"I was a school girl when Randolph Patterson bought that Model T.

51
00:03:00.483 --> 00:03:02.204
Folks didn't like it though.

52
00:03:03.364 --> 00:03:07.946
When that car raced down the road, dust clouds filled the air.

53
00:03:09.047 --> 00:03:10.207
You couldn't breathe.

54
00:03:10.787 --> 00:03:14.309
The farmers, like my daddy, said the dust hurt the crops.

55
00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:20.292
And if it was washing day, the ladies had to take everything off the line.

56
00:03:21.408 --> 00:03:24.431
They had to wash their laundry all over again."

57
00:03:24.451 --> 00:03:30.615
"Your brother is going to drive his Model T in the Willow Creek birthday parade," said Luke.

58
00:03:31.896 --> 00:03:36.200
"Willow Creek is turning 150 years old," said Katie.

59
00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:38.542
"My, my.

60
00:03:38.982 --> 00:03:40.823
Time passes quickly.

61
00:03:41.964 --> 00:03:46.188
When Willow Creek turned fifty, I was just a little girl.

62
00:03:47.336 --> 00:03:51.438
When it turned one hundred, I had gray hair!"

63
00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:53.179
Ms. Henderson laughed.

64
00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:58.221
"And now the town is 150 already?"

65
00:03:58.821 --> 00:04:04.163
"Yep. And we're going to be in the parade," said Emily.

66
00:04:04.183 --> 00:04:06.684
"You could be in it too!"

67
00:04:07.164 --> 00:04:07.885
said Katie.

68
00:04:07.905 --> 00:04:13.667
"Oh, no, I don't go to town anymore," said Ms.

69
00:04:13.687 --> 00:04:15.208
Henderson, shaking her head.

70
00:04:16.492 --> 00:04:18.073
"It's too busy now."

71
00:04:18.093 --> 00:04:21.714
"You could ride in the Model T!"

72
00:04:22.155 --> 00:04:22.875
said AJ.

73
00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:25.896
"We're going," said Emily.

74
00:04:25.916 --> 00:04:31.238
"Well, I have to think about it," said Ms.

75
00:04:31.278 --> 00:04:33.099
Henderson. "Ms.

76
00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:36.581
Henderson, will you write a note for our scavenger bag?"

77
00:04:37.121 --> 00:04:37.881
asked Katie.

78
00:04:39.182 --> 00:04:40.482
Ms. Henderson smiled.

79
00:04:40.502 --> 00:04:44.244
"I did many scavenger hunts when I was a girl."

80
00:04:45.456 --> 00:04:47.078
She happily wrote out a note.

81
00:04:48.279 --> 00:04:51.662
It said: My name is Cora Mae Henderson.

82
00:04:52.242 --> 00:04:54.424
I am 103 years old.

83
00:04:55.745 --> 00:04:57.527
The Earthworms got on their bikes.

84
00:04:57.547 --> 00:05:00.769
"Hope to see you at the parade!"

85
00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:03.812
they called and headed back down the road.

86
00:05:05.313 --> 00:05:06.755
The next morning, Mrs.

87
00:05:06.815 --> 00:05:10.238
Penkov led the campers on a hike along Willow Creek.

88
00:05:11.399 --> 00:05:12.820
She showed them turtle eggs.

89
00:05:13.424 --> 00:05:16.125
She showed them a lizard sleeping in the sun.

90
00:05:17.246 --> 00:05:19.246
The campers picked wildflowers.

91
00:05:20.467 --> 00:05:22.108
Katie was thinking about Ms.

92
00:05:22.128 --> 00:05:27.010
Henderson. Did she walk along the creek when she was eight years old?

93
00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:30.451
What did the creek look like back then?

94
00:05:31.692 --> 00:05:34.053
Suddenly Emily grabbed Katie's arm.

95
00:05:34.633 --> 00:05:35.453
"Did you hear?"

96
00:05:35.933 --> 00:05:36.574
she whispered.

97
00:05:36.594 --> 00:05:42.116
"The Tornadoes are going to the senior home today to look for the oldest person."

98
00:05:43.525 --> 00:05:45.107
"HA!" said Katie.

99
00:05:45.127 --> 00:05:47.292
"They'll never find her there!"
